{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791594519,"nonce":"o2NEI+luxfe4/JJgvmbY/pExArA=","title":"Built-in element behaviours","message":"builtinTags is a list of names. The only behaviour keyed on a tag is focusability (src/native/input.ts), so an a, label, details, progress or form does nothing a browser's would.\n\nPort selectively, cheapest and most useful for the wiki first\n- Lists: each li gets a marker (disc, circle and square by depth; numbers for ol with start, reversed and type), kept right as items come and go. Needs host-owned layout-only children that frameworks do not see in childNodes, since the adapters own their children.\n- a[href]: focusable only with an href, followed by a click or Enter, opens the URL with the system handler, preventDefault honoured.\n- label: a click operates its control (for, or the first input inside) and focuses it.\n- details and summary: toggling the open attribute.\n- progress and meter; fieldset disabled; form with submit, reset and FormData.\n- Later and larger: input (checkbox, radio, range, number, text, validity), select and option with type-ahead, dialog, table with colspan.\n\nReference, for structure: ashui's haxe/ashui/ui/{Lists,Li,Anchor,Label,Details,Summary,Progress,Meter,Fieldset,Form,Input,Select,Dialog,Table}.hx. Most are under 150 lines each.\n\nOpen design question: the adapters (JSX, Vue) own their children, so a marker or a check mark inside an element has to be a node the host owns and the adapter never sees.\n\nAcceptance, per behaviour: an offscreen scene shows it, a pointer or key script drives it, and a framework adapter that re-renders the element keeps it.","files":null}]}